# My Favourite Rainbows

I love rainbows best after a summer storm. The rain stops, the sun peeks out, and suddenly there it is — a big bright arc across the grey sky!

My favourite rainbow appeared last spring. I was walking home from school with my wellies splashing in puddles. The whole street glowed with red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.

But the most magical rainbow I ever saw was a double one! Two rainbows, one above the other, stretched over the fields near my grandad's house. Grandad said the second one was fainter because it was the reflection of the first.

I also love tiny rainbows. Once, I spotted one in the spray from our garden hose. It was small enough to fit in my hands, but just as beautiful as the giant ones.

Some people say there's treasure at the end of a rainbow. I've never found gold, but I think rainbows are treasure enough on their own. They remind me that after every rainy day, something wonderful can appear.

That's why rainbows are my favourite thing in the whole sky! [end of text]


